# Architecture

Use a modular monolith unless the project owner explicitly approves microservices.

Preferred dependency direction:
API -> Application -> Domain
Infrastructure -> Application/Domain
Domain must not depend on Infrastructure or API.

Suggested solution structure:
- `src/Api`
- `src/Application`
- `src/Domain`
- `src/Infrastructure`
- `tests/`

Business rules belong in Domain/Application, not controllers.
Controllers should remain thin.
Infrastructure concerns (Dapper, Npgsql, PostgreSQL, external integrations) stay in Infrastructure. Domain and Application do not reference Dapper, Npgsql, or EF Core.
Avoid generic repositories when they add no value; follow the established project pattern.
Do not create a new abstraction merely to wrap one existing method.
